% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% What the model covers: the toys, games, festive articles, sports
% equipment, fishing tackle and amusements of Chapter 95.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% the model covers the goods of the families of Chapter 95
rule toys_scope_family:
a good is a good the model describes
    if the family of the good is a family
    and the family is a family of chapter ninety-five goods.

toy is a family of chapter ninety-five goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 95, confer "dolls, other toys".
game is a family of chapter ninety-five goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 95, confer "Video game consoles and machines, table or parlor games".
festive article is a family of chapter ninety-five goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 95, confer "Festive, carnival or other entertainment articles, including magic tricks and practical joke articles".
sports equipment is a family of chapter ninety-five goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 95, confer "Articles and equipment for general physical exercise, gymnastics, athletics, other sports (including table-tennis) or outdoor games".
fishing tackle is a family of chapter ninety-five goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 95, confer "Fishing rods, fish hooks and other line fishing tackle".
fairground amusement is a family of chapter ninety-five goods,
    as stated in HTSUS Chapter 95, confer "fairground amusements, including shooting galleries".

% Heading 9503: the tariff's own words, the CN EN and the rulings
tricycle falls in the family toy, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 95, confer "Tricycles, scooters, pedal cars and similar wheeled toys".
scooter falls in the family toy, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 95, confer "Tricycles, scooters, pedal cars and similar wheeled toys".
kick scooter falls in the family toy, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 95, confer "Tricycles, scooters, pedal cars and similar wheeled toys".
pedal car falls in the family toy, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 95, confer "Tricycles, scooters, pedal cars and similar wheeled toys".
wheeled toy falls in the family toy, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 95, confer "Tricycles, scooters, pedal cars and similar wheeled toys".
doll falls in the family toy, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 95, confer "dolls, other toys".
toy falls in the family toy, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 95, confer "dolls, other toys".
toy set falls in the family toy, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 95, confer "dolls, other toys".
toy footwear falls in the family toy, as stated in HTSUS Section XII and Chapter 64, confer "Toy footwear or skating boots with ice or roller skates attached".
doll accessory falls in the family toy, as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 95, confer "clothing, shoes, hats, bags and toiletries for dolls".
doll clothes falls in the family toy, as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 95, confer "clothing, shoes, hats, bags and toiletries for dolls".
scale model falls in the family toy, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 95, confer "and similar recreational models, working or not".
recreational model falls in the family toy, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 95, confer "and similar recreational models, working or not".
model kit falls in the family toy, as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 95, confer "construction sets and constructional toys other than reduced-size ('scale') model assembly kits".
die-cast model falls in the family toy, as stated in ruling NY N244089, confer "The replica car is made of die-cast metal and plastic components".
toy vehicle falls in the family toy, as stated in ruling NY N244089, confer "die-cast toy vehicles".
puzzle falls in the family toy, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 95, confer "puzzles of all kinds".
jigsaw puzzle falls in the family toy, as stated in ruling NY N250079, confer "Both of the items requested contain 100 puzzle pieces".
balloon falls in the family toy, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 95, confer "Inflatable toy balls, balloons and punchballs, of rubber".
toy ball falls in the family toy, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 95, confer "Inflatable toy balls, balloons and punchballs, of rubber".
punchball falls in the family toy, as stated in HTSUS Chapter 95, confer "Inflatable toy balls, balloons and punchballs, of rubber".
anti-stress ball falls in the family toy, as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 95, confer "The 'anti-stress balls' and similar 'anti-stress items' of various shapes and designs are classified in heading 9503".
stuffed toy falls in the family toy, as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 95, confer "Stuffed toys of this subheading usually have an outer fabric of a soft material".
plush toy falls in the family toy, as stated in ruling NY N353849, confer "The plush toy soccer ball is principally designed for the amusement of children 3 years of age and older".
action figure falls in the family toy, as stated in ruling NY N268990, confer "The item provides significant manipulative play value as would any other action figure".
toy figure falls in the family toy, as stated in ruling NY N349980, confer "is described as a toy figurine designed for interactive play".
collectible toy figure falls in the family toy, as stated in ruling NY N286657, confer "two collectible plastic toy dog figurines".
humanoid figurine falls in the family toy, as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 95, confer "These subheadings include humanoid figurines, for example, in the form of film, fairy-tale or comic-book characters".
building blocks falls in the family toy, as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 95, confer "These subheadings also include building blocks".
construction set falls in the family toy, as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 95, confer "These subheadings include construction sets and constructional toys".
toy drone falls in the family toy, as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 95, confer "multi-rotor helicopters (so-called 'drones') of different sizes".
quadcopter falls in the family toy, as stated in ruling NY N323959, confer "it operates like any other remote controlled toy vehicle and provides similar amusement".
remote-control toy falls in the family toy, as stated in ruling NY N323959, confer "it operates like any other remote controlled toy vehicle and provides similar amusement".
remote-control car falls in the family toy, as stated in ruling NY N323959, confer "It is of the same class or kind as other RC vehicles".
remote-control helicopter falls in the family toy, as stated in ruling NY N174717, confer "The item consists of a toy RC helicopter".
fidget toy falls in the family toy, as stated in the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 95, confer "designed to be repeatedly squeezed in the hand as an anti-stress exercise".
