% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Families that do not come from the kind alone.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% Note 3: a part or an accessory suitable for use solely or principally
% with an article of this chapter is classified with that article
rule note_95_3_family with provenance HTSUS Chapter 95,
        confer "parts and accessories which are suitable for use solely or principally with articles of this chapter are to be classified with those articles":
the family of a good is a family
    if the good is a part or accessory suitable for use solely or principally with a kind
    and the kind falls in the family the family
    and the family is a family of chapter ninety-five goods
    and it is not the case that
        the kind is a kind named by note 1 to chapter ninety-five.

% Heading 9505: a decoration made for a festivity is a festive article
% (CN EN: "intended to be used for a specific festivity"; CBP, NY N346694:
% "marketed and sold exclusively as a Christmas decoration")
rule festive_decoration with provenance the CN explanatory notes to Chapter 95,
        confer "These products are, according to their construction and design (imprints, ornaments, symbols or inscriptions), intended to be used for a specific festivity":
the family of a good is festive article
    if the kind of the good is a kind
    and the kind is a kind of decoration
    and the good is marketed as a decoration for a festivity.

% Heading 9506: "including skating boots with skates attached" (a skating
% boot is footwear of Chapter 64 until skates are attached to it)
rule skating_boots_with_skates with provenance HTSUS Chapter 95,
        confer "Ice skates and roller skates, including skating boots with skates attached":
the family of a good is sports equipment
    if the good has ice or roller skates attached.

% Note 4: a toy combined with items of other headings that are no set of
% GRI 3(b), put up together for retail sale, is of heading 9503 if the
% combination has the essential character of toys (the office's judgment)
rule note_95_4 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 95,
        confer "provided the articles are put up together for retail sale and the combinations have the essential character of toys":
the family of a good is toy
    if the good is a combination put up for retail sale with items of other headings
    and the good has the essential character of toys.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The headings (GRI 1).
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

rule heading_9503 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 95,
        confer "Tricycles, scooters, pedal cars and similar wheeled toys":
a good is described by heading 9503
    if the family of the good is toy.

rule heading_9504 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 95,
        confer "Video game consoles and machines, table or parlor games, including pinball machines, billiards, special tables for casino games and automatic bowling equipment":
a good is described by heading 9504
    if the family of the good is game.

rule heading_9505 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 95,
        confer "Festive, carnival or other entertainment articles, including magic tricks and practical joke articles; parts and accessories thereof":
a good is described by heading 9505
    if the family of the good is festive article.

rule heading_9506 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 95,
        confer "Articles and equipment for general physical exercise, gymnastics, athletics, other sports (including table-tennis) or outdoor games, not specified or included elsewhere in this chapter":
a good is described by heading 9506
    if the family of the good is sports equipment.

rule heading_9507 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 95,
        confer "Fishing rods, fish hooks and other line fishing tackle; fish landing nets, butterfly nets and similar nets":
a good is described by heading 9507
    if the family of the good is fishing tackle.

rule heading_9508 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 95,
        confer "Traveling circuses and traveling menageries; amusement park rides and water park amusements; fairground amusements, including shooting galleries; traveling theaters":
a good is described by heading 9508
    if the family of the good is fairground amusement.

% Heading 9506 covers only what no other heading of the chapter specifies
rule heading_9506_residual with provenance HTSUS Chapter 95,
        confer "not specified or included elsewhere in this chapter":
a good is excluded from heading 9506
    if the other heading is in [9503, 9504, 9505, 9507, 9508]
    and the good is described by heading the other heading.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% What bars a good from the chapter's headings: the facts of note 1, notes
% 2 and 5, and the finding that a good is not a toy. These rest on facts
% only, so that the other chapters can read them (below).
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% note 1: the kinds it names
rule note_95_1_kinds with provenance HTSUS Chapter 95, confer "This chapter does not cover:":
a good is barred from heading a heading
    if the heading is in [9503, 9504, 9505, 9506, 9507, 9508]
    and the kind of the good is a kind
    and the kind is a kind named by note 1 to chapter ninety-five.

% note 1(k): parts of general use (Section XV note 2) of base metal, and
% similar goods of plastics
rule note_95_1k with provenance HTSUS Chapter 95,
        confer "Parts of general use, as defined in note 2 to section XV, of base metal (section XV), or similar goods of plastics (chapter 39)":
a good is barred from heading a heading
    if the heading is in [9503, 9504, 9505, 9506, 9507, 9508]
    and the good is a part of general use.

% note 1(x): tableware, kitchenware, toilet articles, apparel, linen and
% similar articles having a utilitarian function; the CN EN excludes from
% heading 9505 the "articles with utilitarian functions"
rule note_95_1x with provenance HTSUS Chapter 95,
        confer "and similar articles having a utilitarian function (classified according to their constituent material)":
a good is barred from heading a heading
    if the heading is in [9503, 9504, 9505, 9506, 9507, 9508]
    and the good has a utilitarian function.

% note 1(c): fishing line not made up is of Chapter 39 or Section XI; the
% fishing line of subheading 9507.90 is "put up and packaged for retail
% sale"
rule note_95_1c with provenance HTSUS Chapter 95,
        confer "Yarns, monofilament, cords or gut or the like for fishing, cut to length but not made up into fishing lines":
a good is barred from heading 9507
    if the kind of the good is fishing line
    and it is not the case that
        the good is put up for retail sale.

% note 2 read with Chapter 71 note 1: the chapter keeps an article whose
% pearls, stones or precious metal are minor constituents only; an article
% with more of them is of Chapter 71
rule note_95_2_metal with provenance HTSUS Chapter 95,
        confer "precious metal or metal clad with precious metal constitute only minor constituents":
a good is barred from heading a heading
    if the heading is in [9503, 9504, 9505, 9506, 9507, 9508]
    and the good contains precious metal beyond minor constituents.

rule note_95_2_stones with provenance HTSUS Chapter 95,
        confer "This chapter includes articles in which natural or cultured pearls, precious or semiprecious stones (natural, synthetic or reconstructed)":
a good is barred from heading a heading
    if the heading is in [9503, 9504, 9505, 9506, 9507, 9508]
    and the good incorporates pearls or stones
    and it is not the case that
        the good has pearls or stones only as minor constituents.

% note 5: pet toys are not of heading 9503
rule note_95_5 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 95,
        confer "Heading 9503 does not cover articles which, on account of their design, shape or constituent material, are identifiable as intended exclusively for animals":
a good is barred from heading 9503
    if the good is identifiable as intended exclusively for animals.

% A toy is principally designed for amusement: a statue that is "not
% principally designed for amusement, but rather serves a utilitarian
% purpose as an article for decoration or display" is no toy (NY N314335).
% A doll is named by the heading itself, and stays a doll when it is made
% for display (NY N366610).
rule toy_amusement with provenance ruling NY N314335,
        confer "we find that the merchandise concerned is not principally designed for amusement, but rather serves a utilitarian purpose as an article for decoration or display":
a good is barred from heading 9503
    if the good is not principally designed for amusement
    and it is not the case that
        the kind of the good is doll.

rule toy_heading_exclusion with provenance HTSUS Chapter 95, confer "This chapter does not cover:":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the good is barred from heading the heading.

% a good of a heading of this chapter: described by it, and not barred
rule good_of_chapter_95 with provenance HTSUS Chapter 95,
        confer "TOYS, GAMES AND SPORTS EQUIPMENT; PARTS AND ACCESSORIES THEREOF":
a good is a good of heading a heading of chapter ninety-five
    if the family of the good is a family
    and the family is a family of chapter ninety-five goods
    and the heading is in [9503, 9504, 9505, 9506, 9507, 9508]
    and the good is described by heading the heading
    and it is not the case that
        the good is barred from heading the heading.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Note 1: the goods it sends to the chapters of the model.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% note 1(d): sports bags and other containers of heading 4202
rule note_95_1d with provenance HTSUS Chapter 95,
        confer "Sports bags or other containers of heading 4202, 4303 or 4304":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading is in [9503, 9504, 9505, 9506, 9507, 9508]
    and the good is described by heading 4202.

% note 1(e) and 1(x): fancy dress, sports clothing and other apparel of
% textiles, of Chapters 61 and 62
rule note_95_1e with provenance HTSUS Chapter 95,
        confer "Fancy dress of textiles, of chapter 61 or 62; sports clothing and special articles of apparel of textiles, of chapter 61 or 62":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading is in [9503, 9504, 9505, 9506, 9507, 9508]
    and the good is described by heading an other heading
    and the other heading >= 6101
    and the other heading <= 6217.

% note 1(g): sports footwear of Chapter 64, other than skating boots with
% ice or roller skates attached
rule note_95_1g with provenance HTSUS Chapter 95,
        confer "Sports footwear (other than skating boots with ice or roller skates attached) of chapter 64":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading is in [9503, 9504, 9505, 9506, 9507, 9508]
    and the other heading is in [6401, 6402, 6403, 6404, 6405, 6406]
    and the good is described by heading the other heading
    and it is not the case that
        the good has ice or roller skates attached.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% The other chapters' notes that send the articles of Chapter 95 here.
% Each rests on "a good of heading H of chapter ninety-five" (described by
% H, and not barred by facts), never on another exclusion.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% Chapter 39 note 2(y)
rule note_39_2y with provenance HTSUS Section VII and Chapter 39,
        confer "Articles of chapter 95 (for example, toys, games, sports equipment)":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading >= 3901
    and the heading <= 3926
    and the good is a good of heading an other heading of chapter ninety-five.

% Chapter 42 note 2(l); a container of heading 4202 stays in Chapter 42
% (Chapter 95 note 1(d))
rule note_42_2l with provenance HTSUS Chapter 42,
        confer "Articles of chapter 95 (for example, toys, games, sports equipment)":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading >= 4201
    and the heading <= 4206
    and the good is a good of heading an other heading of chapter ninety-five
    and it is not the case that
        the good is described by heading 4202.

% Section XI note 1(t); apparel of Chapters 61 and 62 stays there (Chapter
% 95 note 1(e))
rule note_xi_1t with provenance HTSUS Section XI and Chapter 50,
        confer "(t) Articles of chapter 95 (for example, toys, games, sports requisites and nets);":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading >= 5001
    and the heading <= 6310
    and the good is a good of heading an other heading of chapter ninety-five
    and it is not the case that
        the good is described by heading a third heading
        and the third heading >= 6101
        and the third heading <= 6217.

% Chapter 67 note 1(e)
rule note_67_1e with provenance HTSUS Chapter 67,
        confer "Toys, sports equipment, or carnival articles (chapter 95)":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading >= 6701
    and the heading <= 6704
    and the good is a good of heading an other heading of chapter ninety-five.

% Chapter 71 note 3(n): the articles of note 2 to Chapter 95 (a good of
% the chapter is one whose pearls, stones or precious metal are minor
% constituents only, above)
rule note_71_3n with provenance HTSUS Section XIV and Chapter 71,
        confer "Articles covered by note 2 to chapter 95;":
a good is excluded from heading a heading
    if the heading >= 7101
    and the heading <= 7118
    and the good is a good of heading an other heading of chapter ninety-five.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% GRI 6: what the subheadings read.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

% the subheading of what the good is classified as consisting of (GRI
% 3(b)); of several components that equally merit consideration (GRI
% 3(c)), the subheading that occurs last in numerical order (CBP, NY
% N269567: a rod and reel combination goes to the reels)
rule toys_subheading with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "the classification of goods in the subheadings of a heading shall be determined according to the terms of those subheadings and any related subheading notes":
the subheading of a good in heading a heading is a code
    if the heading is in [9503, 9504, 9505, 9506, 9507, 9508]
    and the good is classified as consisting of a component
    and the chapter ninety-five code of the component in heading the heading is the code
    and the numerical order of the code is a number under table subheading order
    and it is not the case that
        the good is classified as consisting of an other component
        and the chapter ninety-five code of the other component in heading the heading is an other code
        and the numerical order of the other code is an other number under table subheading order
        and the other number > the number.

rule toys_code with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "the classification of goods in the subheadings of a heading shall be determined according to the terms of those subheadings and any related subheading notes":
the chapter ninety-five code of a thing in heading a heading is a code
    if the subheading class of the thing is a class
    and the inflation of the thing is a state
    and the payment of the thing is a means
    and the festivity of the thing is a festivity
    and the subheading in heading the heading for the class the class with inflation the state with payment the means with festivity the festivity is the code under table toys and sports.

% the class of a thing: of its kind; of the article it is a part or
% accessory of (note 3); skates attached to boots; otherwise "other"
rule class_by_kind with provenance HTSUS General Rules of Interpretation,
        confer "the classification of goods in the subheadings of a heading shall be determined according to the terms of those subheadings and any related subheading notes":
the subheading class of a thing is a class
    if the kind of the thing is a kind
    and the kind is a kind of the subheading class the class.

rule class_by_part with provenance HTSUS Chapter 95,
        confer "parts and accessories which are suitable for use solely or principally with articles of this chapter are to be classified with those articles":
the subheading class of a thing is a class
    if the thing is a part or accessory suitable for use solely or principally with a kind
    and the kind is a kind of the subheading class the class.

rule class_skates with provenance HTSUS Chapter 95,
        confer "Ice skates and roller skates, including skating boots with skates attached":
the subheading class of a thing is skates
    if the thing has ice or roller skates attached.

rule class_other with provenance HTSUS Chapter 95, confer "Other: 9504.90":
the subheading class of a thing is other
    if it is not the case that
        the kind of the thing is a kind
        and the kind is a kind of the subheading class a class
    and it is not the case that
        the thing is a part or accessory suitable for use solely or principally with an other kind
        and the other kind is a kind of the subheading class a second class
    and it is not the case that
        the thing has ice or roller skates attached.

% subheading 9506.62: inflatable balls
rule inflation_inflatable with provenance HTSUS Chapter 95, confer "Inflatable balls":
the inflation of a thing is inflatable
    if the thing is inflatable.

rule inflation_none with provenance HTSUS Chapter 95, confer "Other: 9506.69":
the inflation of a thing is none
    if the subheading class of the thing is a class
    and it is not the case that
        the thing is inflatable.

% subheading 9504.30 and subheading note 1: games and video game machines
% operated by coins or any other means of payment
rule payment_coins with provenance HTSUS Chapter 95,
        confer "This subheading does not cover video game consoles or machines operated by coins, banknotes, bank cards, tokens or by any other means of payment (subheading 9504.30)":
the payment of a thing is coins
    if the thing is operated by coins or other means of payment.

rule payment_none with provenance HTSUS Chapter 95, confer "Game machines, other than those operated by coins":
the payment of a thing is none
    if the subheading class of the thing is a class
    and it is not the case that
        the thing is operated by coins or other means of payment.

% subheading 9505.10: articles for Christmas festivities
rule festivity_marketed with provenance HTSUS Chapter 95,
        confer "Articles for Christmas festivities and parts and accessories thereof":
the festivity of a thing is a festivity
    if the thing is marketed as a decoration for the festivity.

rule festivity_none with provenance HTSUS Chapter 95, confer "Other: 9505.90":
the festivity of a thing is none
    if the subheading class of the thing is a class
    and it is not the case that
        the thing is marketed as a decoration for a festivity.

% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
% Tests: goods with the facts a reader writes from a ruling.
% ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

query subheading is:
    the subheading of which good is which code.

query heading is:
    the heading of which good is which heading.

query unplaced is:
    which good is not placed by the model.

% Toys of heading 9503 (CBP: the codes the rulings give, at six digits)
scenario toys is:
    % NY N268990: Teenage Mutant Ninja Turtle clip light, an action figure
    % with articulated arms, legs and head -> 9503.00
    the kind of the TMNT clip light is action figure.
    the TMNT clip light is a manufactured article.
    the TMNT clip light is made of plastics.
    % NY N349980: "Booksy", a plastic toy figurine that opens to reveal a
    % tiny comic book -> 9503.00 (Chapter 39 note 2(y): not 3926)
    the kind of Booksy is toy figure.
    Booksy is a manufactured article.
    Booksy is made of plastics.
    % NY N353849: a plush soccer ball of polyester boucle fabric and
    % stuffing -> 9503.00 (a toy, not a ball of 9506)
    the kind of item JF79250WCD is plush toy.
    item JF79250WCD contains 100 percent of polyester.
    % NY N244089: "Welly" replica cars of die-cast metal and plastic -> 9503.00
    the kind of item 18003RW-Yellow is die-cast model.
    % NY N293728: "Max Build More Blocks", 759 interlocking plastic blocks
    % -> 9503.00
    the kind of item 8347 is building blocks.
    item 8347 is a manufactured article.
    item 8347 is made of plastics.
    % NY N323959: a wireless quadcopter with a Wi-Fi camera, not an aircraft
    % of 8806 -> 9503.00
    the kind of CVS item 902411 is quadcopter.
    % NY N174717: "Micro Lightning" remote control helicopter -> 9503.00
    the kind of Costco item 814368 is remote-control helicopter.
    % NY N250079: two jigsaw puzzles of 100 pieces -> 9503.00
    the kind of item IK-3412 is jigsaw puzzle.
    % NY N339261: latex balloons -> 9503.00
    the kind of the latex balloons is balloon.
    % NY N340079: American Girl "Styling Set for Doll", 34 pieces for doll
    % hairstyles -> 9503.00
    the kind of item GPV22 is doll accessory.
    % NY N366610: a handmade collectable doll for display only -> 9503.00 (a
    % doll is named by the heading; Chapter 97 does not apply)
    the kind of Armand is doll.
    Armand is not principally designed for amusement,
        according to CBP, because "This item is not intended for children's play but rather for display purposes only".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of the TMNT clip light is 9503.00", "the subheading of Booksy is 9503.00", "the subheading of item JF79250WCD is 9503.00", "the subheading of item 18003RW-Yellow is 9503.00", "the subheading of item 8347 is 9503.00", "the subheading of CVS item 902411 is 9503.00", "the subheading of Costco item 814368 is 9503.00", "the subheading of item IK-3412 is 9503.00", "the subheading of the latex balloons is 9503.00", "the subheading of item GPV22 is 9503.00", "the subheading of Armand is 9503.00"].

% Sets and composite goods of heading 9503
scenario toy_sets is:
    % NY N286657: "Chubby Puppies and Friends", two collectible plastic toy
    % dog figurines and a doughnut-shaped holder, a set whose essential
    % character the figurines give -> 9503.00
    the Chubby Puppies set is a set put up for retail sale.
    the figurines of the Chubby Puppies set is a component of the Chubby Puppies set.
    the holder of the Chubby Puppies set is a component of the Chubby Puppies set.
    the kind of the figurines of the Chubby Puppies set is collectible toy figure.
    the figurines of the Chubby Puppies set is made of plastics.
    the holder of the Chubby Puppies set is made of plastics.
    the essential character of the Chubby Puppies set is given by the figurines of the Chubby Puppies set,
        according to CBP, because "The essential character is imparted by the toy dog figurines".
    % NY N347069: Monster High doll with a stand, a plastic pet cobra and
    % paper posters (the large poster de minimis) -> 9503.00
    the kind of item JDR65 is doll.
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of the Chubby Puppies set is 9503.00", "the subheading of item JDR65 is 9503.00"].

% Games of heading 9504
scenario games is:
    % NY N217140: "Atari Flashback 4", a console with built-in games that
    % plugs into a television -> 9504.50
    the kind of item 9017710 is video game console.
    % NY N327482: wired controllers for the Nintendo Switch -> 9504.50; the
    % wireless controller is radio remote control apparatus (note 1(m), 8526)
    the kind of model NSAC0069-01 is video game controller.
    the kind of model NSAC0072-01 is wireless video game controller.
    % NY N329078: plastic grips for wireless controllers: no accessory of an
    % article of Chapter 95, so of Chapter 39 -> 3926.90
    the C2Gripz is a part or accessory suitable for use solely or principally with wireless video game controller.
    the C2Gripz is a manufactured article.
    the C2Gripz is made of plastics.
    the principal use of the C2Gripz is other use,
        according to CBP, because "This product is a dedicated accessory for a wireless game controller".
    % NY N352820: Yu-Gi-Oh! trading cards of paper -> 9504.40
    the kind of the Yu-Gi-Oh cards is trading cards.
    % NY N336171: 48 foam dice -> 9504.90
    the kind of model PT166 is dice.
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of item 9017710 is 9504.50", "the subheading of model NSAC0069-01 is 9504.50", "the subheading of the C2Gripz is 3926.90", "the subheading of the Yu-Gi-Oh cards is 9504.40", "the subheading of model PT166 is 9504.90"].
    unplaced expects answers ["model NSAC0072-01 is not placed by the model"].

% Festive articles of heading 9505
scenario festive is:
    % NY N346694: a glass nutcracker figurine sold exclusively as a
    % Christmas decoration -> 9505.10
    the kind of item BCZW2024006L is figurine.
    item BCZW2024006L is marketed as a decoration for Christmas,
        confer "The item is marketed and sold exclusively as a Christmas decoration for the home".
    % NY N302865: artificial Christmas trees of polyvinyl chloride -> 9505.10
    the kind of model 9043390 is artificial Christmas tree.
    model 9043390 is a manufactured article.
    model 9043390 is made of plastics.
    % NY N353478: a wooden tabletop decoration in the shape of vampire lips,
    % sold as a decoration for Halloween -> 9505.90
    the kind of SKU BCLF22895H-1 is decoration.
    SKU BCLF22895H-1 is marketed as a decoration for Halloween,
        confer "The item will be marketed and sold as a decoration for Halloween".
    % NY N340898: "Paw Patrol Birthday Yard Decor Kit", flimsy printed yard
    % signs for a birthday party -> 9505.90
    the kind of style OEM23-0833 is yard sign.
    style OEM23-0833 is marketed as a decoration for birthday,
        confer "The single-use item will be marketed and sold as a party decoration".
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of item BCZW2024006L is 9505.10", "the subheading of model 9043390 is 9505.10", "the subheading of SKU BCLF22895H-1 is 9505.90", "the subheading of style OEM23-0833 is 9505.90"].

% Sports equipment of heading 9506
scenario sports is:
    % NY N357738: a yoga mat of polyvinyl chloride -> 9506.91
    the kind of item YS-STICKY-6MM-SG is yoga mat.
    item YS-STICKY-6MM-SG is a manufactured article.
    item YS-STICKY-6MM-SG is made of plastics.
    % NY N233886: Everlast jump ropes -> 9506.91
    the kind of item JMP1U is jump rope.
    % NY N346125: Element Popsicle skateboard -> 9506.99
    the kind of SKU 51795 is skateboard.
    % NY N303881: regulation golf balls -> 9506.32; plastic golf tees ->
    % 9506.39 (the same heading, so no set)
    the kind of the golf balls of CVS item 285697 is golf ball.
    the kind of the golf tees of CVS item 285697 is golf tee.
    % NY N346126: "Gem Roller Skates", roller skates with adjustable boots
    % -> 9506.70
    the kind of SKU 51207 is roller skate.
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of item YS-STICKY-6MM-SG is 9506.91", "the subheading of item JMP1U is 9506.91", "the subheading of SKU 51795 is 9506.99", "the subheading of the golf balls of CVS item 285697 is 9506.32", "the subheading of the golf tees of CVS item 285697 is 9506.39", "the subheading of SKU 51207 is 9506.70"].

% Fishing tackle of heading 9507
scenario fishing is:
    % NY N365995: a metal casting lure of brass and lead with one hook: the
    % lure gives the essential character -> 9507.90
    the Hoko lure is a composite good.
    the lure of the Hoko lure is a component of the Hoko lure.
    the hook of the Hoko lure is a component of the Hoko lure.
    the kind of the Hoko lure is fishing lure.
    the kind of the lure of the Hoko lure is fishing lure.
    the kind of the hook of the Hoko lure is fish hook.
    the essential character of the Hoko lure is given by the lure of the Hoko lure,
        according to CBP, because "Since the hook cannot perform its ultimate function without the lure, the lure imparts the essential character to the complete article".
    % NY N283135: tungsten worm sinkers -> 9507.90
    the kind of the worm sinkers is fishing sinker.
    % NY N269567: "Alpha Spin Combo Fishing Rod", a rod with a reel attached,
    % equally essential: GRI 3(c), the reel occurs last -> 9507.30
    the Alpha Spin Combo is a composite good.
    the rod of the Alpha Spin Combo is a component of the Alpha Spin Combo.
    the reel of the Alpha Spin Combo is a component of the Alpha Spin Combo.
    the kind of the Alpha Spin Combo is fishing rod.
    the kind of the rod of the Alpha Spin Combo is fishing rod.
    the kind of the reel of the Alpha Spin Combo is fishing reel.
    the essential character of the Alpha Spin Combo is given by no single component,
        according to CBP, because "Being that the reel and the rod are equally essential to the article's performance, no essential character can be determined".
    % NY N340501: a boat landing net on an aluminum pole -> 9507.90
    the kind of item UL-31-P is landing net.
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of the Hoko lure is 9507.90", "the subheading of the worm sinkers is 9507.90", "the subheading of the Alpha Spin Combo is 9507.30", "the subheading of item UL-31-P is 9507.90"].

% Goods the chapter does not take: a statue for display (NY N314335), a
% cycling glove (note 1(w); NY N233894 classifies it in 6116), and the
% facts of note 1 and note 5
scenario exclusions is:
    % NY N314335: a plastic statue of a video game character on a base, not
    % principally designed for amusement -> 3926.40 (not 9503)
    the kind of the Ellie statue is humanoid figurine.
    the Ellie statue is a manufactured article.
    the Ellie statue is made of plastics.
    the Ellie statue is not principally designed for amusement,
        according to CBP, because "we find that the merchandise concerned is not principally designed for amusement".
    the principal use of the Ellie statue is ornament,
        according to CBP, because "serves a utilitarian purpose as an article for decoration or display".
    % NY N233894: a knitted cycling glove: note 1(w) keeps it out of Chapter 95
    the kind of the RL Liner is cycling glove.
    % note 5: a toy identifiable as intended exclusively for animals
    the kind of toy A is toy.
    toy A is identifiable as intended exclusively for animals.
    % note 1(w): a racket string is no accessory of heading 9506
    the kind of string B is racket string.
    string B is a part or accessory suitable for use solely or principally with tennis racket.
    % note 1(x): a festive article with a utilitarian function
    the kind of ornament C is Christmas ornament.
    ornament C has a utilitarian function.
    subheading expects answers ["the subheading of the Ellie statue is 3926.40"].
    unplaced expects answers ["toy A is not placed by the model", "string B is not placed by the model", "ornament C is not placed by the model"].

% The subheadings the rulings above do not reach, and notes 1(d), 3 and 4
scenario subheadings is:
    the kind of ball A is basketball.
    the kind of ball B is baseball.
    the kind of ball C is baseball.
    ball C is inflatable.
    the kind of game D is pinball machine.
    game D is operated by coins or other means of payment.
    the kind of game E is video game console.
